          "turn_index": 1,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Is that high?",
          "answer": "I can't tell you whether 58 is high. The guidance I found doesn't give the cut-off values for HbA1c, and it doesn't say which units your result uses.\n\n- **The only number I found is a general goal.** The glycemic-targets document describes an HbA1c below 7 percent as a reasonable goal for many adults who already have type 2 diabetes. It is a treatment goal, not a test threshold, and it only applies if the scale is percent. (*Type 2 diabetes: glycemic targets and monitoring intervals*)\n- **Units matter.** HbA1c is reported either as a percentage or in mmol/mol, and the two scales give very different numbers. A value of 58 could mean quite different things on each. Check the units on your report.\n- **The screening document didn't return its thresholds.** The type 2 diabetes screening guidance was listed, but its text didn't come back, so I can't quote the cut-offs for normal, prediabetes or diabetes.\n\nPlease ask your clinician or the lab that issued the report what 58 means in your case, which units it uses, and whether it should be repeated.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
